[2026-09-24] c:5824099852 comment by w0xlt (contributor):
`ValidateBlock()` can make the node connect an invalid block.

It caches successful script checks in `m_script_execution_cache`, whose key is the wtxid and the script flags. It doesn't include the coins being spent. That's safe for coins from the UTXO set, since an outpoint always refers to the same output. With `ValidateBlock()`, though, the caller supplies the coins and can return anything.

For example, a `CoinFetcher` that returns an `OP_TRUE` script instead of the real one gets the transaction cached as valid. A later `ProcessBlock()` on the same chainman then reuses that result and connects the block, even though it fails against the real UTXO set. Later `ValidateBlock()` calls with wrong coins also pass.

This only happens with 0 script check worker threads, which is the kernel default. When the checks run on worker threads, nothing gets cached.

The tests below reproduce both cases, along with a suggested fix: don't cache results in `ConnectBlock()` when it's called from `ValidateBlock()`.

